\section{Per-reach calibration data}\label{si:perreach}
Table~\ref{tab:si-reach} reports, for each of the 20 gauged reaches, the
station-maximum observed PFOS, the calibrated modeled concentration
(soil-loading $=0.11$, no point source), and the $5$th--$95$th-percentile predictive
envelope from the 120-member ensemble. ``M'' marks the seven Rogue mainstem reaches
(stream order $\geq4$); ``T'' marks the thirteen tributary reaches. The envelope
brackets the observation on six of seven mainstem reaches and almost no tributary
reaches---the basis for the $P$-factor decomposition in the main text.

